    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Apologies for the confusion. There is indeed a direct shinkansen line from Osaka to Fukuoka, which is called the Takayama Line. Departing from Shin-Osaka Station and arriving at Hakata Station, it takes roughly 2 hours and 12 minutes. This service is indeed direct and offers a very convenient journey between Osaka and Fukuoka with minimal transfers, making it one of the most efficient options for inter-city travel in Japan.\n\nFocusing on a smooth and stress-free journey, the direct Shinkansen from Osaka to Fukuoka should certainly help in minimizing chaos, avoiding long hurried transfers, and reducing the possibility of getting lost. It's also well-engineered, so the chances of unexpected delays are low, though trains are always subject to some minor delays, including weather-related ones. Regularly checking the Sangi Express app will give users real-time updates and a reliable travel experience.\n\nBy choosing the direct Sangi Express, you prioritize convenience, comfort, and in this case, avoiding the possibility of confusion from more complicated routes with multiple stations on the line. Plus, you'll save time and have more time to explore the cities or rest during your visit.",
